From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noswad <64293615+TheNoswad@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 15:12:41 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Input: add the Cirrus Logic CS40L2x haptics driver (Google
 vendor)

The Pixel 6 haptics amplifier (CS40L25A) has no mainline driver. This is
the cs40l2x driver from Google's amplifiers kernel module
(android.googlesource.com/kernel/google-modules/amplifiers, branch
android-gs-raviole-6.1-android16, commit 33976d763bc0), GPL-2.0, ported:

- builds against this kernel (no init_name rename, 48 B firmware block
  writes the regmap accepts),
- input force feedback: FF_RUMBLE/FF_PERIODIC are mapped to the stock
  waveforms (< 50 ms: click, index 2 level 66; longer: long, index 0
  level 56 scaled by magnitude), no mutex in the FF playback callback
  (it runs under the input event lock),
- vendor headers kept inside the driver directory.
---
 drivers/input/misc/Kconfig                    |     2 +
 drivers/input/misc/Makefile                   |     1 +
 drivers/input/misc/cs40l2x/Kconfig            |    15 +
 drivers/input/misc/cs40l2x/Makefile           |     4 +
 drivers/input/misc/cs40l2x/cs40l2x-tables.c   |  1172 ++
 drivers/input/misc/cs40l2x/cs40l2x.c          | 12042 ++++++++++++++++
 .../include/linux/mfd/cs40l25-wavetable.h     |    62 +
 .../misc/cs40l2x/include/linux/mfd/cs40l2x.h  |  1569 ++
 .../include/linux/platform_data/cs40l2x.h     |    73 +
 9 files changed, 14940 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/input/misc/cs40l2x/Kconfig
 create mode 100644 drivers/input/misc/cs40l2x/Makefile
 create mode 100644 drivers/input/misc/cs40l2x/cs40l2x-tables.c
